cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APTpy, please cite the toolbox release used and cite APAV separately."
type: software
title: "APTpy: A Graphical Python Toolbox for Atom-Probe Tomography Data Analysis"
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/APTpy/APTpy"
authors:
  - family-names: "Aliabad"
    given-names: "Roohallah Surki"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  APTpy combines graphical candidate-ion exploration, range-file creation,
  and isotope-constrained overlap analysis for atom-probe tomography mass
  spectra. The toolbox is an independent companion project built on APAV.
keywords:
  - atom-probe tomography
  - mass spectrum
  - isotope analysis
  - range files
  - Python
  - graphical user interface
